Notebook[{Cell["Transverse spin transfer in proton-proton collisions, step 1: \
diagrams and amplitudes of one class", "Title"], 
  Cell["Single-inclusive parton production in proton-proton collisions with \
the incoming parton a transversely polarized and the transverse spin of the \
observed parton c measured, a(pa)^ + b(pb) -> c(p)^ + X, at NLO in QCD for \
the seven channel classes of classes.wl (docs/TRANSVERSE-PP.md).  The \
variable class below selects the class (1, 3, 6, 10, 11, 13, 17); every step \
of this process starts with it, and the results are stored under \
Results/<route>/class-<n>/.\n\nThe diagrams and amplitudes do not know about \
the spin: this step is that of Processes/Hadronic (read its 1-Amplitudes.wl), \
for the classes of this process.  For the chosen class it generates with \
FeynArts the Born process a b -> c d (when it exists), its one-loop \
corrections, and every real-emission process a b -> c d e of the class with \
its weight, and converts the amplitudes into plain records.  In addition it \
generates the Born amplitudes of the 2 -> 2 transfer channels listed in \
classes.wl (TransferBornChannels), whose D-dimensional \
transverse-spin-transfer squares step 2 computes for the collinear \
counterterms of step 4 (Processes/Hadronic reads that table from \
Processes/PartonicBorn; here the table depends on the spin projections of \
this process and is built with its own machinery).\n\nMomenta: pa, pb \
incoming; p the observed parton; k1, k2 the unobserved partons (k1 + k2 = pa \
+ pb - p); loop the loop momentum.  Flavours: q = quark of flavour i (up \
quark of FeynArts' SMQCD model), qp = quark of flavour k (charm), g = gluon; \
closed quark loops run over all three generations of the model and are \
counted with the symbol Nf in step 2.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Load the package and the class", "Section"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \
\"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["LoadFeynCalc[]", "Input"], 
  Cell["class = \"1\";\nGet[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"classes.wl\"}]];\nRequire[KeyExistsQ[HadronicTransferClasses, \
ToExpression[class]], \"Not a class of the transverse spin transfer\", \
class];\nspec = HadronicTransferClasses[ToExpression[class]];\nPrint[\"Class \
\", class, \": \", spec[\"Name\"]];\nspec", "Input"], 
  Cell["Generate the diagrams", "Section"], Cell["FeynArts fields: F[3,{1}] \
the up quark (flavour i), F[3,{2}] the charm quark (flavour k), V[5] the \
gluon, U[5] the gluon ghost (only in loops).  Everything else of the SMQCD \
model (photon, weak bosons, Higgs, leptons, down-type quarks, the third \
generation as an external particle) is excluded.  The observed parton is the \
first outgoing particle of each process; the tadpole topologies and the \
self-energy corrections on external legs are excluded from the one-loop \
generation (they are scaleless and vanish for massless partons).", "Text"], 
  Cell["field = <|\"q\" -> F[3, {1}], \"qb\" -> -F[3, {1}], \"qp\" -> F[3, \
{2}], \"qpb\" -> -F[3, {2}], \"g\" -> V[5]|>;\nexcluded = {S[_], V[1 | 2 | \
3], F[1 | 2 | 4]};\ngenerate[loops_, in_, out_] := \
InsertFields[CreateTopologies[loops, Length[in] -> Length[out],\n    \
ExcludeTopologies -> If[loops == 0, {}, {Tadpoles, WFCorrections}]],\n  \
(field /@ in) -> (field /@ out), InsertionLevel -> {Classes}, Model -> \
\"SMQCD\",\n  ExcludeParticles -> Join[excluded, If[loops == 0, {U[_]}, \
{}]]];\nbornDiagrams = If[spec[\"Born\"] === None, None, generate[0, \
spec[\"Born\"][[1 ;; 2]], spec[\"Born\"][[3 ;; 4]]]];\nvirtualDiagrams = \
If[spec[\"Virtual\"], generate[1, spec[\"Born\"][[1 ;; 2]], spec[\"Born\"][[3 \
;; 4]]], None];\nrealDiagrams = Association @ Table[StringRiffle[proc[[1]], \
\" \"] -> generate[0, proc[[1]][[1 ;; 2]], proc[[1]][[3 ;; 5]]], {proc, \
spec[\"Real\"]}];\n<|\"Born\" -> If[bornDiagrams === None, 0, \
Length[bornDiagrams]], \"Virtual\" -> If[virtualDiagrams === None, 0, \
Length[virtualDiagrams]],\n  \"Real\" -> Map[Length, realDiagrams]|>", 
   "Input"], Cell["If[bornDiagrams =!= None, Paint[bornDiagrams, ColumnsXRows \
-> {Min[Length[bornDiagrams], 4], 1}, Numbering -> Simple, SheetHeader -> \
None, ImageSize -> {170 Min[Length[bornDiagrams], 4], 170}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["The transfer Born channels for the counterterms: the unobserved \
parton d of a b -> c d follows from flavour conservation (it is unique for \
every channel of the list).", "Text"], Cell["flavourNumber[x_] := Switch[x, \
\"q\", {1, 0}, \"qb\", {-1, 0}, \"qp\", {0, 1}, \"qpb\", {0, -1}, \"g\", {0, \
0}];\npartner[{a_, b_, c_}] := Module[{ok = Select[Keys[field], \
Total[flavourNumber /@ {a, b}] === Total[flavourNumber /@ {c, #}] &]},\n  \
Require[Length[ok] == 1, \"The unobserved parton of \" <> a <> \" \" <> b <> \
\" -> \" <> c <> \" is not unique\", ok]; First[ok]];\nchannelName[{a_, b_, \
c_}] := a <> \" \" <> b <> \" -> \" <> c;\ntableDiagrams = Association @ \
Table[channelName[ch] -> generate[0, ch[[1 ;; 2]], {ch[[3]], partner[ch]}], \
{ch, TransferBornChannels}];\nMap[Length, tableDiagrams]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Amplitudes", "Section"], Cell["FCFAConvert rewrites the FeynArts \
amplitudes in FeynCalc notation without contracting anything; quark masses \
are set to zero, the gauge parameter to one (Feynman gauge).  The one-loop \
amplitudes keep the loop momentum loop.  The third-generation quark running \
in closed loops appears with the symbolic FeynArts generation sum, which step \
2 replaces by the number of flavours Nf.", "Text"], 
  Cell["convert[diagrams_, in_, out_, loops_: {}] := \
FCFAConvert[CreateFeynAmp[diagrams, Truncated -> False, PreFactor -> 1],\n  \
IncomingMomenta -> in, OutgoingMomenta -> out, LoopMomenta -> loops, \
UndoChiralSplittings -> True, ChangeDimension -> D,\n  List -> True, SMP -> \
False, Contract -> False, DropSumOver -> False,\n  FinalSubstitutions -> \
{FCGV[\"MU\"] -> 0, FCGV[\"MC\"] -> 0, FCGV[\"MT\"] -> 0, SMP[\"g_s\"] -> \
gs}] /. GaugeXi[_] -> 1 /. MQU[_] -> 0;   (* MQU: mass of the loop quark of \
generic generation *)\namplitudes = <|\n  \"Born\" -> If[bornDiagrams === \
None, {}, convert[bornDiagrams, {pa, pb}, {p, k1}]],\n  \"Virtual\" -> \
If[virtualDiagrams === None, {}, convert[virtualDiagrams, {pa, pb}, {p, k1}, \
{loop}]],\n  \"Real\" -> Map[convert[#, {pa, pb}, {p, k1, k2}] &, \
realDiagrams],\n  \"BornTable\" -> Map[convert[#, {pa, pb}, {p, k1}] &, \
tableDiagrams]|>;\nLength /@ Append[Map[Length, amplitudes[\"Real\"]], \
\"Virtual\" -> amplitudes[\"Virtual\"]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Closed quark loops: FeynArts sums the generation index of a closed \
fermion loop (SumOver[Index[Generation, n], 3]); the loop amplitudes are the \
same for every massless flavour, so each such amplitude counts Nf times.  \
Amplitudes with an external-generation sum do not occur because every \
external flavour is fixed.", "Text"], Cell["flavourSum = \
SumOver[Index[Generation, _], 3] -> Nf;\nRequire[FreeQ[amplitudes, \
SumOver[Index[Generation, _], _, External]], \"An external generation sum \
appeared\"];\namplitudes = amplitudes /. flavourSum /. SumOver[__] -> 1;      \
(* the colour sums are implicit in the colour algebra of step 2 \
*)\nCount[amplitudes[\"Virtual\"], Nf, Infinity]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Records", "Section"], Cell["records = <|\"Born\" -> AmplitudeRecords \
/@ amplitudes[\"Born\"], \"Virtual\" -> AmplitudeRecords /@ \
amplitudes[\"Virtual\"],\n  \"Real\" -> Map[AmplitudeRecords /@ # &, \
amplitudes[\"Real\"]], \"BornTable\" -> Map[AmplitudeRecords /@ # &, \
amplitudes[\"BornTable\"]]|>;\nRequire[FreeQ[records, $Failed], \"A record \
could not be formed\"];\nweights = Association @ \
Table[StringRiffle[proc[[1]], \" \"] -> proc[[2]], {proc, \
spec[\"Real\"]}];\nSaveAmplitudes[<|\"FeynCalc\" -> amplitudes, \"Records\" \
-> records, \"Class\" -> class, \"Spec\" -> spec, \"Weights\" -> weights,\n  \
\"TransferBornChannels\" -> Map[channelName, TransferBornChannels]|>, \
\"class-\" <> class];\nShowRecords[Flatten[records[\"Born\"]]]", "Input"]}, 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
